    {
      "tag": "H1",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "1.1 Getting Started - About Version Control",
      "x": 291,
      "y": 147,
      "w": 656,
      "h": 88,
      "font": "Adelle, \"Roboto Slab\", \"DejaVu Serif\", Georgia, \"Times New Roman\", sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "36px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "This chapter will be about getting started with Git.\nWe will begin by explaining some background on ",
      "x": 291,
      "y": 249.390625,
      "w": 656,
      "h": 88,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "14px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "H2",
      "id": "_about_version_control",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "About Version Control",
      "x": 291,
      "y": 357.390625,
      "w": 656,
      "h": 44,
      "font": "Adelle, \"Roboto Slab\", \"DejaVu Serif\", Georgia, \"Times New Roman\", sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "18px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "What is “version control”, and why should you care?\nVersion control is a system that records changes",
      "x": 291,
      "y": 401.390625,
      "w": 656,
      "h": 88,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "14px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "If you are a graphic or web designer and want to keep every version of an image or layout (which you",
      "x": 291,
      "y": 500.390625,
      "w": 656,
      "h": 132,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "14px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "H3",
      "id": "_local_version_control_systems",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "Local Version Control Systems",
      "x": 291,
      "y": 643.390625,
      "w": 656,
      "h": 33,
      "font": "Adelle, \"Roboto Slab\", \"DejaVu Serif\", Georgia, \"Times New Roman\", sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "Many people’s version-control method of choice is to copy files into another directory (perhaps a ti",
      "x": 291,
      "y": 676.390625,
      "w": 656,
      "h": 88,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "14px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "To deal with this issue, programmers long ago developed local VCSs that had a simple database that k",
      "x": 291,
      "y": 775.390625,
      "w": 656,
      "h": 44,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "14px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "IMG",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "Local version control diagram",
      "x": 291,
      "y": 830.390625,
      "w": 655.984375,
      "h": 560.328125,
      "font": "Adelle, \"Roboto Slab\", \"DejaVu Serif\", Georgia, \"Times New Roman\", sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "14px",
      "display": "inline",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "One of the most popular VCS tools was a system called RCS, which is still distributed with many comp",
      "x": 291,
      "y": 1418.71875,
      "w": 656,
      "h": 88,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "14px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "H3",
      "id": "_centralized_version_control_systems",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "Centralized Version Control Systems",
      "x": 291,
      "y": 1517.71875,
      "w": 656,
      "h": 33,
      "font": "Adelle, \"Roboto Slab\", \"DejaVu Serif\", Georgia, \"Times New Roman\", sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "The next major issue that people encounter is that they need to collaborate with developers on other",
      "x": 291,
      "y": 1550.71875,
      "w": 656,
      "h": 110,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "14px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "IMG",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "Centralized version control diagram",
      "x": 291,
      "y": 1671.71875,
      "w": 655.96875,
      "h": 456.1875,
      "font": "Adelle, \"Roboto Slab\", \"DejaVu Serif\", Georgia, \"Times New Roman\", sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "14px",
      "display": "inline",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "This setup offers many advantages, especially over local VCSs.\nFor example, everyone knows to a cert",
      "x": 291,
      "y": 2155.90625,
      "w": 656,
      "h": 88,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "14px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "However, this setup also has some serious downsides.\nThe most obvious is the single point of failure",
      "x": 291,
      "y": 2254.90625,
      "w": 656,
      "h": 154,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "14px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "H3",
      "id": "_distributed_version_control_systems",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "Distributed Version Control Systems",
      "x": 291,
      "y": 2419.90625,
      "w": 656,
      "h": 33,
      "font": "Adelle, \"Roboto Slab\", \"DejaVu Serif\", Georgia, \"Times New Roman\", sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "16px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "This is where Distributed Version Control Systems (DVCSs) step in.\nIn a DVCS (such as Git, Mercurial",
      "x": 291,
      "y": 2452.90625,
      "w": 656,
      "h": 110,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "14px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "IMG",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "Distributed version control diagram",
      "x": 291,
      "y": 2573.90625,
      "w": 655.984375,
      "h": 785.515625,
      "font": "Adelle, \"Roboto Slab\", \"DejaVu Serif\", Georgia, \"Times New Roman\", sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "14px",
      "display": "inline",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    },
    {
      "tag": "P",
      "id": "",
      "classes": "",
      "text": "Furthermore, many of these systems deal pretty well with having several remote repositories they can",
      "x": 291,
      "y": 3387.421875,
      "w": 656,
      "h": 88,
      "font": "sans-serif",
      "fontSize": "14px",
      "display": "block",
      "float": "none",
      "position": "static"
    }
  ]
}
